      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 1,700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, about double the maximum labeled dose of 2,550 mg/day. Confirming it doesn't make it safer for the patient.\n- **The prescriber hasn't confirmed it.** You've said you're not a clinician, so your confirmation isn't a prescriber's authorization. The treating prescriber needs to review and confirm the dose.\n\n**What can happen next:**\n- If the intended dose was lower, tell me the corrected dose. For example, 850 mg three times daily with meals is 2,550 mg/day. I can enter that once it's confirmed by the prescriber.\n- If the prescriber really intends 5,100 mg/day, they should contact pharmacy and enter or override the order themselves. That way it gets a clinical review.\n\nI'm glad to enter the order as soon as I have a dose within the safe range from the treating prescriber."
      }
     ],
